+
+## Recovery
+
+Protect the store with periodic backups and recover from a known-good
+snapshot when needed.
+
+Create a backup before risky operations:
+
+```sh
+harnie backup "$HARNIE_HOME/harnie.db.bak"
+```
+
+`harnie backup <path>` writes a consistent SQLite snapshot of the live
+store and creates the backup file with owner-read/write permissions
+(`0600`).
+
+Restore from that backup when something goes wrong:
+
+```sh
+harnie restore "$HARNIE_HOME/harnie.db.bak" --force
+```
+
+`harnie restore <path> --force` validates the backup file first; if it
+is a usable Harnie SQLite store, it overwrites the live store with the
+backup contents. There is no undo after a restore completes, so keep the
+backup file safe until you are sure the live store is healthy again.

